{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqda7rpovti","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gate worktree enforcement gap: metric-only check misses regular parallel subagents","summary":"The orch-gate hooks (orch-gate.sh + orch-gate-bash.sh) only enforce orch/attempt/* branch isolation when the claimed task has a metric spec (HAS_METRIC check). Regular parallel subagents with valid non-metric claims are allowed to write to any branch — including main — causing concurrent agents to overwrite each other's work.\n\nFix: replace the HAS_METRIC conditional with an IS_SUB check in the claimed block. If is_subagent==true AND not on orch/attempt/*, block with: \"call branch_task before editing\". Drop the /task/detail curl round-trip (no longer needed). Update parallel-orchestrate/SKILL.md and CLAUDE.md gate contract to include branch_task as a required step after start_task.\n\n**Why:** The hold-merge/worktree isolation shipped in a6a3552b only hardened the infrastructure (leases, GC guard) and the loop skill instructions. It never updated the gate to hard-enforce isolation for human-dispatched parallel tasks.\n\n**How to apply:** All subagent prompts must include branch_task after start_task. The gate will hard-block any subagent write not on orch/attempt/*.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T04:26:09.804Z","vec":[-0.04340708628296852,-0.028593547642230988,-0.021491823717951775,-0.030206555500626564,0.014181369915604591,-0.06804326176643372,-0.022223908454179764,-0.016877325251698494,0.03135206550359726,0.08105139434337616,0.01020073052495718,-0.07522141933441162,-0.02090396359562874,-0.009828024543821812,0.013457727618515491,-0.0029681765008717775,-0.0020729845855385065,-0.02263401821255684,-0.08911652863025665,-0.0846066102385521,0.014644812792539597,0.032732557505369186,0.038496293127536774,0.07648227363824844,-0.06259801238775253,-0.04987906292080879,-0.07057128101587296,0.0004496202163863927,-0.006885972805321217,-0.0006488221697509289,-0.0470366217195